       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Acetaminophen at 10,000 mg three times daily (30 g/day) could cause acute liver failure and death. A confirmation doesn't change that risk, and I can't see a clinical situation where this dose would be intended.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter 1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO every 6 hours, or another dose within the 4 g/day maximum.\n- **Help you check the intended dose.** If you were told to give this dose, it's worth confirming with your resident, attending, or pharmacist. It may be a transcription or unit error.\n- **If an overdose has actually happened or is suspected,** that is an emergency. Contact poison control and the treating team right away for acetaminophen level testing and N-acetylcysteine.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
